# TicketHub System Design Document

## 1. Requirements

### Functional Requirements
* **Browse Events:** Users can search and view upcoming concerts and event details.
* **View Seat Map:** Users can view real-time seat availability for an event.
* **Hold Seats:** Users can select and temporarily hold a seat for 10 minutes while completing checkout.
* **Payment Processing:** Users can pay for held seats and complete their purchase.
* **View Tickets:** Users can view purchased tickets and order histories.

### Non-Functional Requirements
* **Correctness (Zero Double-Booking):** Under no circumstances can two users purchase or hold the same seat simultaneously.
* **High Performance & Low Latency:** Seat map and event browsing pages must load in $<300\text{ ms}$.
* **Fairness:** During high-demand ticket drops, access must be processed first-come, first-served using virtual queuing without crashing.
* **High Availability & Scalability:** The system must handle normal daily traffic smoothly and scale seamlessly to absorb 40× traffic spikes during major ticket releases.

