## 2. Capacity & Traffic Estimates

### Starting Facts
* **Registered Users:** 2,000,000 (2 Million)
* **Normal Day:** 50,000 visitors, 10 page views/user, 5,000 tickets sold/day.
* **Big Sale Drop:** 200,000 users attempting to buy 20,000 seats within a 10-minute (600-second) window.

### Normal Day Calculations
* **Daily Page Views:** 
  $$50,000 \text{ visitors} \times 10 \text{ pages} = 500,000 \text{ views/day}$$
* **Average Reads per Second:** 
  $$\frac{500,000}{86,400 \text{ seconds}} \approx 5.79 \text{ QPS}$$
* **Average Writes (Ticket Purchases) per Second:** 
  $$\frac{5,000}{86,400 \text{ seconds}} \approx 0.058 \text{ WPS}$$

### "Big Sale" Peak Calculations (10-Minute Window)
* **Peak Visitors:** 200,000 users in 600 seconds.
* **Peak Request Rate (assuming 1 request/sec per user browsing/holding):** 
  $$\frac{200,000 \text{ users}}{600 \text{ seconds}} \approx 333.33 \text{ requests/sec}$$
* **Peak Write Attempts (Purchases/Holds over 10 mins):** 
  $$\frac{200,000 \text{ checkout attempts}}{600 \text{ seconds}} \approx 333.33 \text{ write attempts/sec}$$

### Traffic Comparison
* **Traffic Multiplier:** Read requests jump from **5.79 QPS** on a normal day to over **333.33 QPS** during a big sale (approx. **57× increase**).
* **Write Multiplier:** Write traffic jumps from **0.058 WPS** to **333.33 WPS** (approx. **5,700× increase**).

